# E30 PingPong: parallel benchmark, durations ignored. Compared: five trials in order, one count of messages, one
# duration and one rate (three decimals) each, and the bounds of the counts: never more than the limit of 10 000 000
# plus the few sends that pass the check at the same time. The C# reaches its 10 000 turns first (2 to 3 million
# messages per trial in .NET 10), the C++ reaches the limit: the counts themselves are not compared.
ignore ^$
cover all
fact trial ^Trial (\d)$
fact messages ^(\d+) msg$
fact duration ^\d+ ms$
fact rate ^\d+\.\d{3} msg/ms$
same trial seq
same messages count
same duration count
same rate count
check trial count == 5
check messages max(0) <= 10000010
check messages min(0) >= 90
